  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "The records collectively identify the relevant Al-Co-Cr-Fe-Ni FCC/B2 lamellar systems, show that thermal or thermomechanical processing can change their phase morphology, and establish that coherent and hierarchical phase architectures can improve strength and ductility in HEAs. In particular, R17 demonstrates coherent interfaces in a nearly identical alloy, while R5, R11, and R19 connect coherent or hierarchical multiphase structures with improved mechanical properties. Other records supply related deformation mechanisms such as dislocation activity, stacking faults, twinning, transformation plasticity, and multistage strain hardening. However, none describes HPHT treatment of the eutectic Al0.7CoCrFeNi alloy, conversion of its lamellae into the reported hierarchical pattern, or preferential dislocation transfer across coherent FCC/B2 interfaces. Thus the literature points in the right direction, but selecting HPHT and predicting its specific interface-mediated mechanism would require a substantial new idea."
